<#
.SYNOPSIS
    Provides a Get-Weather function that retrieves weather data by ZIP code.

.DESCRIPTION
    Defines a Get-Weather function that queries the CDYNE WeatherWS SOAP web service
    using New-WebServiceProxy and returns current weather information for the given US
    ZIP code.

.PARAMETER ZipCode
    The US ZIP code for which to retrieve weather information.

.NOTES
    Author: David Cook
    - The CDYNE Weather web service (wsf.cdyne.com) may not be active or publicly
      available. Verify the endpoint before use.
    - New-WebServiceProxy requires Windows PowerShell (not PowerShell Core).

.EXAMPLE
    Import the module and call Get-Weather:
    . .\WeatherFunctions.psm
    Get-Weather -ZipCode "66101"
    Returns current weather data for ZIP code 66101 (Kansas City, KS).
#>
function Get-Weather{
   param ([String]$ZipCode)
   $b = New-WebServiceProxy -Uri http://wsf.cdyne.com/WeatherWS/Weather.asmx?wsdl
   $b.GetCityWeatherByZIP($ZipCode)
}
